{
  "A six-month residency for artists who make Omarchy beautiful. Themes, plugins, and whatever else. The point is to let creativity flow with the support of the Omacom Foundation. Up to five seats at any one time.": "为让 Omarchy 更美的艺术家提供六个月驻留计划。主题、插件，或任何其他作品。目标是在 Omacom Foundation 的支持下，让创造力自由流淌。同期最多五个名额。",
  "The first residents": "首批驻留艺术家",
  "<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Solitude and Last Horizon</a> both ship with Omarchy, and another twenty of his themes sit on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a> - more than anyone else has contributed: Batou, Oxo Carbon, Velvet Night, Rose of Dune, Shades of Jade, and on it goes. He&rsquo;s a mechanical engineer who became one of the defining aesthetic forces in this community, sits on <a href=\"/teams/\">Omarchy Core</a>, and helps steward <a href=\"https://plugins.omarchy.org/\">the plugin ecosystem</a>.": "<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Solitude 和 Last Horizon</a> 都已内置于 Omarchy，<a href=\"/themes/\">额外主题页面</a>还有他的二十款作品，比任何人贡献的都多：Batou、Oxo Carbon、Velvet Night、Rose of Dune、Shades of Jade，等等。他从机械工程师成为社区审美的关键推动者，是 <a href=\"/teams/\">Omarchy Core</a> 成员，也参与维护<a href=\"https://plugins.omarchy.org/\">插件生态</a>。",
  "Three of the themes that ship with Omarchy are his - <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Lumon, Miasma, and Retro 82</a> - and another ten sit on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a>, from Batman to City-783 to Sakura Mochi. He works in whole palettes rather than one-off colour schemes, which is why his themes hold together across the terminal, Neovim, btop, and the shell instead of just looking good in a screenshot.": "三款内置主题出自他手：<a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Lumon、Miasma 和 Retro 82</a>。<a href=\"/themes/\">额外主题页面</a>还有十款，从 Batman、City-783 到 Sakura Mochi。他设计完整的调色板，而非一次性的配色，因此主题在终端、Neovim、btop 和 shell 中都协调一致，不只是截图好看。",
  "He drew the Omarchy logo, which is reason enough, and he built <a href=\"https://github.com/tahayvr/omarchist\">Omarchist</a>, the GUI for making your own themes without touching a config file. <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Matte Black</a> is his and ships with Omarchy, along with Gold Rush, Sunset Drive, and VHS 80 on <a href=\"/themes/\">the extras page</a>.": "他绘制了 Omarchy 标志，仅这一点就足够了；他还开发了 <a href=\"https://github.com/tahayvr/omarchist\">Omarchist</a>，让你不碰配置文件就能制作主题的图形工具。内置的 <a href=\"/manual/themes/\">Matte Black</a> 出自他手，<a href=\"/themes/\">额外主题页面</a>还有 Gold Rush、Sunset Drive 和 VHS 80。",
  "Remaining seats by invitation": "其余名额采用邀请制",
  "What it comes with": "我们提供什么",
  "<span><strong>$2,500/month</strong> for the full six months.</span>": "<span>整个六个月，每月提供 <strong>2,500 美元</strong>。</span>",
  "<span><strong>Token account</strong> so the agents never need to stop.</span>": "<span><strong>Token 账户</strong>，让智能体无需停工。</span>",
  "<span><strong>Permanent recognition</strong> as AIR alumni when six months are up.</span>": "<span>六个月结束后，作为 AIR 校友获得<strong>永久认可</strong>。</span>",
  "The nonprofit funding the development, maintenance, and spread of Omarchy.<br>Interested in becoming a founding or distinguished patron? Write <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>.": "资助 Omarchy 开发、维护与传播的非营利基金会。<br>有兴趣成为创始或杰出赞助人？请联系 <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "Patrons": "赞助人",
  "The foundation is funded by its patrons: twelve Founding Patrons contributing $1,000,000 each, Distinguished Patrons at $100,000, Distinguished Corporate Patrons at $100,000 a year - and soon a tier open to everyone.": "基金会由赞助人支持：十二位创始赞助人各捐助 1,000,000 美元，杰出赞助人各捐助 100,000 美元，杰出企业赞助人每年捐助 100,000 美元，很快还将开放人人可参与的等级。",
  "Sponsorships": "项目资助",
  "Multi-year sponsorships for the projects Omarchy is built on - Hyprland, Quickshell, and mise - so the people behind them can work without thinking about fundraising.": "为 Omarchy 所依赖的 Hyprland、Quickshell 和 mise 提供多年资助，让开发者专注工作，不必为筹款操心。",
  "Artists in Residence": "驻留艺术家",
  "Omarchy AIR pays artists a six-month stipend to work freely on themes, plugins, and whatever else makes the system beautiful.": "Omarchy AIR 为艺术家提供六个月津贴，让他们自由创作主题、插件，以及任何能让系统更美的作品。",
  "<a href=\"#founding-patrons\">Founding Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#founding-patrons\">创始赞助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $1,000,000.": "每位捐助 1,000,000 美元。",
  "<a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">Elite capital. Public code.</a>": "<a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">精英的资本。大众的代码。</a>",
  "<a href=\"#founding-token-patrons\">Founding Corporate Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#founding-token-patrons\">创始企业赞助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $1,000,000/year for three years or $1,500,000 in tokens with option for refill.": "每家每年捐助 1,000,000 美元，持续三年；或提供可追加的 1,500,000 美元 token。",
  "<a href=\"#distinguished-patrons\">Distinguished Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#distinguished-patrons\">杰出赞助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $100,000.": "每位捐助 100,000 美元。",
  "<a href=\"#distinguished-corporate-patrons\">Distinguished Corporate Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#distinguished-corporate-patrons\">杰出企业赞助人</a>",
  "Each contributing $100,000/year for three years or $150,000 in tokens with option for refill.": "每家每年捐助 100,000 美元，持续三年；或提供可追加的 150,000 美元 token。",
  "<a href=\"#become-a-patron\">Become a Founding or Distinguished Patron</a>": "<a href=\"#become-a-patron\">成为创始或杰出赞助人</a>",
  "Interested in becoming a founding or distinguished patron? Write <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>.": "有兴趣成为创始或杰出赞助人？请联系 <a href=\"mailto:david@omarchy.org\">david@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "<a href=\"#everyone\">All Patrons</a>": "<a href=\"#everyone\">全部赞助人</a>",
  "Each contributing as they see fit. Open for everyone.<br><a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">Become a patron</a> and <a href=\"/patrons/badges/\">collect your badge</a>.": "按自己的意愿捐助，向所有人开放。<br><a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">成为赞助人</a>，<a href=\"/patrons/badges/\">领取徽章</a>。",
  "Every patron of the Omacom Foundation gets a digital rally credential to show for it. There's a badge for your website, a card for your socials, and wallpapers for your desktop and your phone. Four classes, one for each <a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">tier of patronage</a>. Pick your stage!": "每位 Omacom Foundation 赞助人都能获得一份数字拉力赛凭证。包括网站徽章、社交卡片，以及桌面和手机壁纸。四个组别，对应四档<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">赞助等级</a>。选好你的赛段！",
  "Forest Stage &middot; $16": "森林赛段 &middot; 16 美元",
  "The entry class. Green foil, gravel flying, and a Quattro heading into the trees. Sixteen bucks gets you on the team.": "入门组。绿色箔光、飞溅的砂石，一辆 Quattro 驶入林间。十六美元就能加入车队。",
  "Mountain Hairpin &middot; $256": "山地发卡弯 &middot; 256 美元",
  "Blue foil and a dusty hairpin high up the mountain. This is the class for those who want to put some real weight behind the mission.": "蓝色箔光，高山发卡弯上扬起的尘土。为愿意给这项使命提供有力支持的人准备。",
  "Service Park &middot; $2,048": "维修区 &middot; 2,048 美元",
  "Violet foil under the floodlights of the service park, where the car gets rebuilt between stages. Two thousand dollars keeps a lot of open-source developers in the race.": "维修区灯光下的紫色箔光，赛车在赛段之间重新整备。两千美元能让许多开源开发者继续参赛。",
  "Night Stage &middot; $8,192": "夜间赛段 &middot; 8,192 美元",
  "Magenta foil, four headlights, and a night stage carved out of the mountainside. The top class of open patronage. Thank you!": "洋红色箔光、四盏头灯，以及沿山坡开辟的夜间赛道。公开赞助中的最高组别。谢谢你！",
  "<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">Become a patron</a> to claim yours. Artwork by <a href=\"https://github.com/OldJobobo\">OldJobobo</a>, <a href=\"/air/\">Artist in Residence</a>.": "<a href=\"https://donate.omarchy.org\">成为赞助人</a>即可领取。作品来自<a href=\"/air/\">驻留艺术家</a> <a href=\"https://github.com/OldJobobo\">OldJobobo</a>。",
  "Report a vulnerability": "报告漏洞",
  "If you believe you&rsquo;ve found a security vulnerability in Omarchy, please tell the <a href=\"/teams/#security\">Omarchy Security Team</a> privately so we have an opportunity to investigate and fix it before it is made public.": "如果你认为发现了 Omarchy 安全漏洞，请私下告知 <a href=\"/teams/#security\">Omarchy Security 团队</a>，让我们有机会在公开前调查并修复。",
  "Please don&rsquo;t report potential vulnerabilities publicly in GitHub Issues, Discord, or social media before they&rsquo;ve been resolved.": "请不要在问题解决前，将潜在漏洞公开发布到 GitHub Issues、Discord 或社交媒体。",
  "What is a vulnerability?": "什么是漏洞？",
  "We consider a bug a security vulnerability when it can be exploited to cross a meaningful security boundary: an untrusted or lower-privileged party gains access, permissions, or control they didn&rsquo;t already have.": "当一个错误可被利用来跨越实质性的安全边界时，我们将其视为安全漏洞：不受信任或权限较低的一方，获得原本不具备的访问权、权限或控制能力。",
  "Code that could be more robust but does not cross a security boundary is an improvement rather than a security vulnerability. We may still merge a proposed fix and credit the reporter in our release notes.": "可以更健壮、但不跨越安全边界的代码属于改进事项，而非安全漏洞。我们仍可能合入修复，并在发行说明中感谢报告者。",
  "Eligibility for our <a href=\"/security/credits/\">security credits</a> page depends on whether a report identifies a confirmed security vulnerability, not on its severity.": "能否列入<a href=\"/security/credits/\">安全贡献者</a>页面，取决于报告是否指出了经确认的安全漏洞，而不是漏洞的严重程度。",
  "What to include": "报告应包含什么",
  "Give us enough information to understand and reproduce the issue:": "请提供足够的信息，让我们理解并复现问题：",
  "The affected component and Omarchy version.": "受影响的组件与 Omarchy 版本。",
  "An explanation of what an attacker can do before and after exploitation.": "说明攻击者在利用漏洞前后分别能做什么。",
  "Steps to reproduce the issue and any proof of concept.": "复现步骤，以及任何概念验证代码。",
  "Your preferred contact details for follow-up.": "你希望用于后续沟通的联系方式。",
  "Responsible disclosure": "负责任的披露",
  "Please act in good faith while investigating and reporting vulnerabilities:": "调查和报告漏洞时，请秉持善意：",
  "Only test systems and accounts you own or have explicit permission to test.": "仅测试你拥有或获得明确授权的系统与账户。",
  "Avoid privacy violations, disruption, data destruction, and service degradation.": "避免侵犯隐私、造成中断、破坏数据或降低服务质量。",
  "Don&rsquo;t exploit a vulnerability beyond what is needed to demonstrate it.": "不要超出证明漏洞所必需的范围进行利用。",
  "Give us a reasonable opportunity to investigate and address the issue before publishing details.": "公开详情前，请给我们合理的调查与处理机会。",
  "We&rsquo;ll review your report and keep you informed as we&rsquo;re able while we work toward a resolution.": "我们会审阅报告，并在解决问题期间尽可能向你更新进展。",
  "Credits": "致谢",
  "Researchers who privately report a confirmed security vulnerability and give us the chance to ship a fix are thanked on the <a href=\"/security/credits/\">security credits</a> page. Accepted improvements that don&rsquo;t cross a security boundary may still be credited in our release notes.": "私下报告已确认的安全漏洞，并让我们有机会发布修复的研究者，将获列入<a href=\"/security/credits/\">安全贡献者</a>页面。未跨越安全边界但被采纳的改进，也可能在发行说明中获得致谢。",
  "Credits link to each reporter&rsquo;s X profile and show their avatar. For duplicate reports, only the first reporter is eligible for credit.": "致谢会展示报告者头像并链接其 X 主页。对于重复报告，仅首位报告者可获列名。",
  "Regular bugs and support": "普通错误与求助",
  "For anything that isn&rsquo;t a security vulnerability, please use the <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues\">Omarchy issue tracker</a>.": "对于非安全漏洞的问题，请使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues\">Omarchy 问题跟踪器</a>。",
  "They found it, told us privately, and waited for the patch": "他们发现问题，私下告知，并等待补丁",
  "Found something? <a href=\"/security/\">Report it privately</a>. The first reporter of a confirmed vulnerability is credited here.": "发现了什么？请<a href=\"/security/\">私下报告</a>。首位报告已确认漏洞的人会在这里获得致谢。",
  "Exclusive": "独家",
  "The tiling Wayland compositor that has been at the heart of Omarchy since day one, and one of its three core technologies. The sponsorship lets Vaxry work on it without having to think about commercial development or fundraising - and it freed the existing Hyprperks program to be released for everyone, for free. The deal runs three years, with an option for another two, and starts October 10.": "这款平铺式 Wayland 合成器从第一天起就是 Omarchy 的核心，也是三大基础技术之一。赞助让 Vaxry 无需考虑商业开发或筹款，专心投入，也让现有 Hyprperks 得以免费向所有人开放。协议从 10 月 10 日开始，为期三年，可再延长两年。",
  "Premier": "主要",
  "The desktop construction kit the Omarchy shell is built on: one long-running process drawing the bar, the menu, the notifications, the OSDs and the lock screen. It shipped in Quattro, and over a thousand plugins followed in the first week. Termed for three years out the gate.": "Omarchy shell 的桌面构建工具包：一个常驻进程绘制状态栏、菜单、通知、OSD 和锁屏。它随 Quattro 推出，第一周就出现了超过一千款插件。协议一开始便签订三年。",
  "The tool that manages the language runtimes and, just as importantly, ships every coding-agent CLI as a lazy-loading stub. A new harness is one command away instead of a packaging project - which is what keeps Omarchy moving at the pace agent tooling actually ships.": "这款工具管理语言运行时，同样重要的是，它把每个编程智能体 CLI 都作为按需加载的启动器提供。新的智能体环境只需一条命令，而不用另做打包项目，这正是 Omarchy 能跟上智能体工具发布节奏的原因。",
  "A 2011 ThinkPad X220. Just 2GB of RAM. Watch Omarchy run with room to spare.": "2011 年的 ThinkPad X220，仅有 2GB 内存。看看 Omarchy 如何游刃有余地运行。",
  "David Heinemeier Hansson takes Omarchy for a spin on a very modest machine.": "David Heinemeier Hansson 在一台配置十分朴素的电脑上试用 Omarchy。",
  "You don't need a new computer to try Omarchy. Give the one you already have a second life.": "试用 Omarchy 不需要新电脑。让手头的老机器焕发新生。",
  "Coming 2026": "将于 2026 年推出",
  "Early Aesthetics": "早期美学",
  "There's only so much you can do with GNOME, but I did what I could.": "GNOME 能做的有限，但我尽力了。",
  "Neovim and Zellij out of the box.": "开箱即用的 Neovim 和 Zellij。",
  "Even then, one command could re-theme multiple apps.": "即使在当时，一条命令也能为多个应用更换主题。",
  "The road to Omarchy": "通往 Omarchy 的路",
  "Omakub proved the thesis: give developers a beautiful, complete Linux out of the box, and they&rsquo;ll show up! Tens of thousands did.": "Omakub 证明了这个想法：给开发者一个开箱即用、美观完整的 Linux，他们就会来！数万人来了。",
  "But it also found the ceiling. Omakub was a layer of opinion on top of Ubuntu and GNOME, and those come with strong opinions of their own. The ideas I actually cared about - tiling, everything on the keyboard, a system that treats the terminal as the center of the universe - kept fighting the platform instead of flowing from it.": "但它也碰到了天花板。Omakub 在 Ubuntu 和 GNOME 之上叠加自己的主张，而它们本身也有很强的主张。我真正关心的东西——平铺窗口、全键盘操作、以终端为宇宙中心的系统——总是在与平台对抗，而不是从平台自然生长。",
  "So the omakase moved from Ubuntu to Arch, from GNOME to Hyprland, and became <a href=\"/\">Omarchy</a>. Not a layer on top of somebody else&rsquo;s distribution, but the whole meal. Everything Omakub was reaching for, without asking anyone&rsquo;s permission first.": "于是，omakase 从 Ubuntu 转向 Arch，从 GNOME 转向 Hyprland，成为 <a href=\"/\">Omarchy</a>。不再只是别人发行版上的一层，而是整桌菜。Omakub 想实现的一切，无需先征求任何人的许可。",
  "The retirement home is staffed": "退休之后，也有人照看",
  "Omakub itself is now retired. The repositories are archived on GitHub - <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub\">omakub</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub-site\">omakub-site</a>. But good ideas don&rsquo;t retire, they get forked! <a href=\"https://omabuntu.omakasui.org/\">Omabuntu</a> is a community fork continuing on the omakase-Ubuntu thread. If Arch is a step too far and Ubuntu is home, that&rsquo;s where you should go.": "Omakub 现已退休。GitHub 仓库 <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub\">omakub</a> 和 <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omakub-site\">omakub-site</a> 已归档。但好想法不会退休，只会被分叉！<a href=\"https://omabuntu.omakasui.org/\">Omabuntu</a> 是延续 omakase-Ubuntu 路线的社区分支。如果 Arch 跨度太大，而 Ubuntu 才是熟悉的家，那就去那里。",
  "Thanks to everyone who ran it, contributed to it, and showed off their desktops. Omakub walked so Omarchy could run.": "感谢所有使用它、贡献它、展示自己桌面的人。Omakub 学会了走，Omarchy 才能奔跑。",
  "Wordmark": "文字标识",
  "OMA Logo": "OMA 标志",
  "Trademark": "商标",
  "Omarchy is a pending trademark. All rights reserved.": "Omarchy 商标正在申请中。保留所有权利。",
  "Write <a href=\"mailto:foundation@omarchy.org\">foundation@omarchy.org</a> for partnerships.": "合作请联系 <a href=\"mailto:foundation@omarchy.org\">foundation@omarchy.org</a>。",
  "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-badge.png\">Badge</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-social.png\">Social card</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-wallpaper.jpg\">Desktop wallpaper</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-mobile.jpg\">Mobile wallpaper</a>": "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-badge.png\">徽章</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-social.png\">社交卡片</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-wallpaper.jpg\">桌面壁纸</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/016/open-omarchy-016-mobile.jpg\">手机壁纸</a>",
  "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-badge.png\">Badge</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-social.png\">Social card</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-wallpaper.jpg\">Desktop wallpaper</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-mobile.jpg\">Mobile wallpaper</a>": "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-badge.png\">徽章</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-social.png\">社交卡片</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-wallpaper.jpg\">桌面壁纸</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/256/open-omarchy-256-mobile.jpg\">手机壁纸</a>",
  "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-badge.png\">Badge</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-social.png\">Social card</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-wallpaper.jpg\">Desktop wallpaper</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-mobile.jpg\">Mobile wallpaper</a>": "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-badge.png\">徽章</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-social.png\">社交卡片</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-wallpaper.jpg\">桌面壁纸</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/2K/open-omarchy-2K-mobile.jpg\">手机壁纸</a>",
  "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-badge.png\">Badge</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-social.png\">Social card</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-wallpaper.jpg\">Desktop wallpaper</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-mobile.jpg\">Mobile wallpaper</a>": "<a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-badge.png\">徽章</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-social.png\">社交卡片</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-wallpaper.jpg\">桌面壁纸</a> &middot; <a href=\"/assets/images/badges/8K/open-omarchy-8K-mobile.jpg\">手机壁纸</a>",
  "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-exclusive-hyprland-sponsor/\">Read the announcement</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://hypr.land/\">Hyprland</a> by <a href=\"https://x.com/vaxryy\">Vaxry</a>": "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-exclusive-hyprland-sponsor/\">阅读公告</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://hypr.land/\">Hyprland</a>，作者 <a href=\"https://x.com/vaxryy\">Vaxry</a>",
  "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-premier-mise-sponsor/\">Read the announcement</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://mise.jdx.dev/\">mise</a> by <a href=\"https://x.com/jdxcode\">jdx</a>": "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-premier-mise-sponsor/\">阅读公告</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://mise.jdx.dev/\">mise</a>，作者 <a href=\"https://x.com/jdxcode\">jdx</a>",
  "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-premier-quickshell-sponsor/\">Read the announcement</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a> by <a href=\"https://x.com/outfoxxedd\">outfoxxed</a>": "<a href=\"/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-to-be-premier-quickshell-sponsor/\">阅读公告</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a>，作者 <a href=\"https://x.com/outfoxxedd\">outfoxxed</a>",
  "Logo": "标志",
  "<a href=\"/news/2026/09/omacom-foundation-hires-outfoxxed/\">Read the announcement</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a> by <a href=\"https://x.com/outfoxxedd\">outfoxxed</a>": "<a href=\"/news/2026/09/omacom-foundation-hires-outfoxxed/\">阅读公告</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a> 作者 <a href=\"https://x.com/outfoxxedd\">outfoxxed</a>",
  "Full-time Omacom Foundation employee": "Omacom Foundation 全职员工",
  "Head of Omarchy Kernel": "Omarchy Kernel 负责人",
  "Head of Omarchy Shell": "Omarchy Shell 负责人",
  "Krzysztof co-maintains key parts of Linux&rsquo;s PCI subsystem. His work helps the kernel communicate with modern hardware, from graphics cards to fast storage. He leads Omarchy Kernel performance, compatibility, and security, and serves on <a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a>.": "Krzysztof 共同维护着 Linux PCI 子系统的关键部分。他的工作帮助内核与现代硬件顺畅协作，从显卡到高速存储。他负责 Omarchy Kernel 的性能、兼容性和安全性，并在 <a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a> 任职。",
  "Multi-year sponsorships for the projects Omarchy is built on - Hyprland and mise - so the people behind them can work without thinking about fundraising.": "为 Omarchy 所基于的项目——Hyprland 和 mise——提供多年期赞助，让背后的开发者可以专心工作，不用为筹款操心。",
  "Quickshell is the desktop construction kit behind Omarchy Shell. It provides the building blocks for bars, menus, notifications, widgets, and lock screens, using QML to turn ideas into interfaces that update as you work. That flexibility lets people and their agents build plugins and shape the desktop around their needs. Its creator, outfoxxed, is a full-time Omacom Foundation employee as Head of Omarchy Shell and a member of Omarchy Core, working to make the shell and its foundations faster, more reliable, and easier to extend.": "Quickshell 是 Omarchy Shell 背后的桌面构建工具包。它为状态栏、菜单、通知、小组件和锁屏提供构建模块，用 QML 把想法变成随工作实时更新的界面。这种灵活性让用户和他们的智能体可以构建插件，按自己的需求打造桌面。它的创建者 outfoxxed 是 Omacom Foundation 的全职员工，担任 Omarchy Shell 负责人，也是 Omarchy Core 成员，致力于让 shell 及其基础更快、更可靠、更易于扩展。",
  "Staff": "员工",
  "The Omacom Foundation employees working full time on Omarchy.": "全职为 Omarchy 工作的 Omacom Foundation 员工。",
  "The full-time employees of the Omacom Foundation, paid for by <a href=\"/patrons/\">our patrons</a> to make Omarchy better for everyone.": "Omacom Foundation 的全职员工，由<a href=\"/patrons/\">我们的赞助人</a>资助，让 Omarchy 为每个人变得更好。",
  "outfoxxed created <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a>, the toolkit behind Omarchy Shell. He makes the desktop faster, more reliable, and easier for people and agents to extend through plugins. He also serves on <a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a>.": "outfoxxed 创建了 <a href=\"https://quickshell.org/\">Quickshell</a>，这是 Omarchy Shell 背后的工具包。他让桌面更快、更可靠，并让用户和智能体可以通过插件轻松扩展。他同时在 <a href=\"/teams/#core\">Omarchy Core</a> 任职。",
  "The people and companies funding the development, maintenance, and spread of Omarchy.": "资助 Omarchy 开发、维护和推广的个人与公司。",
  "Head of Infrastructure": "基础设施负责人",
  "<a href=\"#welcome-the-agents\">Welcome the agents</a>": "<a href=\"#welcome-the-agents\">欢迎智能体</a>",
  "The modern history of computers is barely a lifetime old, but its heritage is rich and deserves our respect. It&#39;s our duty to honor those who forged the path before us. From <a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/10307\">shipping basic vi</a> fifty years after Bill Joy wrote the first version to dedicating a <a href=\"https://github.com/dhh/omarchy-giants-theme\">theme to von Neumann</a>. We should be proud of how we got here and make our ancestors smile from retirement or above.": "现代计算机的历史不过短短一辈子的时间，但它的传承丰厚，值得我们尊敬。致敬前人开辟的道路是我们的责任。从 Bill Joy 写出第一个版本五十年后我们还在<a href=\"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/pull/10307\">默认搭载基础版 vi</a>，到为 von Neumann 献上<a href=\"https://github.com/dhh/omarchy-giants-theme\">专属主题</a>。我们应该为自己如何走到今天而自豪，让祖师爷们在退休中或在天上露出微笑。",
  "<a href=\"#perfect-the-computer\">Perfect the computer</a>": "<a href=\"#perfect-the-computer\">打造完美电脑</a>",
  "There&#39;s no paper cut too small, no incompatibility too difficult, and no partnership that&#39;s out of reach. Omarchy&#39;s mission is nothing less than <em>The Perfect Computer</em>. That means <a href=\"https://x.com/mitchellh/status/2074225453217505494\">the pursuit of excellence without justification</a>. Everything should be faster, better, prettier. We can do all of it, at the same time, and be done before ASI.": "没有小到不值得修的纸片级毛病，没有难到搞不定的兼容问题，也没有够不着的合作。Omarchy 的使命就是 <em>完美电脑</em>。这意味着<a href=\"https://x.com/mitchellh/status/2074225453217505494\">不讲理由地追求卓越</a>。一切都要更快、更好、更美。我们可以同时搞定所有事，还能在 ASI 到来之前完工。",
  "<a href=\"#have-some-fun\">Have some fun</a>": "<a href=\"#have-some-fun\">找点乐子</a>",
  "<a href=\"#beauty-is-truth\">Beauty is truth</a>": "<a href=\"#beauty-is-truth\">美即真理</a>",
  "The age of agents is the most important paradigm shift in computing since the microprocessor, and Omarchy is going to take full advantage. Agents are welcome everywhere. In the code, in the issues, in the pull requests, and in the infrastructure. We&#39;re going to lean all the way in, put the new intelligence to work all over, and together <a href=\"https://wecanfixeverything.com\">We Can Fix Everything</a>!": "智能体时代是自微处理器以来计算领域最重要的范式转变，Omarchy 要全力拥抱。智能体处处受欢迎。在代码里，在 issues 里，在 pull requests 里，在基础设施里。我们要全力投入，把新的智能用在每个角落，一起 <a href=\"https://wecanfixeverything.com\">We Can Fix Everything</a>！",
  "<a href=\"#heritage-is-duty\">Heritage is duty</a>": "<a href=\"#heritage-is-duty\">传承即责任</a>",
  "<a href=\"#hold-the-line\">Hold the line</a>": "<a href=\"#hold-the-line\">守住底线</a>",
  "<a href=\"#own-the-machine\">Own the machine</a>": "<a href=\"#own-the-machine\">拥有你的机器</a>",
  "<a href=\"#youre-somebody-now\">You&#39;re somebody now</a>": "<a href=\"#youre-somebody-now\">你现在可是个人物了</a>",
  "There are amazing nerds everywhere. Cracked teenagers. Wise neckbeards. Obsessive people with jagged opinions and incredible talent. But we&#39;re spread across a thousand little fiefdoms, accomplishing a fraction of what we could together. Omarchy is a rallying cry to unite that talent behind a common goal: Make Linux win the desktop, as the prophecy foretold.": "牛人到处都有。开挂的少年。睿智的老鸟。偏执又有惊人天赋的人。但我们分散在一千个小山头里，取得的成就远不及团结起来能做到的。Omarchy 就是团结这些人才的集结号，共同实现一个目标：让 Linux 赢得桌面，正如预言所说。",
  "We&#39;re serious people, doing serious work, but if we can&#39;t laugh at ourselves and the delusional mission, it gets stuffy and stale real quick. We need fun, we need whimsy, we need cool for its own sake. The computer needs easter eggs, it needs silly games, it needs <a href=\"https://radio.omarchy.org\">funny pun songs</a>. Serious people have serious fun.": "我们是做正经事的正经人，但如果不能自嘲一下、笑一笑这个疯狂的使命，气氛很快就会又闷又无聊。我们需要乐趣，需要奇思妙想，需要为酷而酷。电脑需要彩蛋，需要傻乎乎的小游戏，需要<a href=\"https://radio.omarchy.org\">搞笑的双关歌曲</a>。正经人也要正经地玩。",
  "<a href=\"#command-is-service\">Command is service</a>": "<a href=\"#command-is-service\">命令即服务</a>",
  "<a href=\"#unite-the-nerds\">Unite the nerds</a>": "<a href=\"#unite-the-nerds\">团结极客</a>",
  "The Perfect Computer may start as omakase, but it&#39;s ultimately yours. Fully and completely. No tollbooths, no gatekeepers, no platforms that can change the terms on you. Just free and open code that you can turn into whatever you desire. The malleable machine of the future is here today and it&#39;s yours to own.": "完美电脑也许始于 omakase，但它最终完全彻底属于你。没有收费站，没有守门人，没有能单方面改规则的平台。只有自由开放的代码，你可以把它变成任何你想要的样子。未来那台可塑的机器，今天就在这里，归你所有。",
  "Omarchy is for everyone willing to learn and participate. From <a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">billionaires</a> to anons on X. From <a href=\"/staff\">staff engineers</a> to script kiddies. From <a href=\"https://omarchy.cn\">China</a> to Malibu. Show up, fix something, or just spread the enthusiasm. <a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2097747649625497874\">You&#39;re somebody now</a>.": "Omarchy 属于每一个愿意学习和参与的人。从 <a href=\"https://oligarchy.fyi\">亿万富翁</a>到 X 上的匿名网友。从 <a href=\"/staff\">资深工程师</a>到脚本小子。从 <a href=\"https://omarchy.cn\">中国</a>到 Malibu。来露个面，修点东西，或者只是传播这份热情。<a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2097747649625497874\">你现在可是个人物了</a>。",
  "Great tools are beautiful because they&#39;re right. The best curve of the blade is also the elegant one, so let&#39;s nail the sharp lines of that TUI, get those corner radii right, and polish the CLIs. The colors should be coordinated. The padding should be just so. There&#39;s enough desaturated brutalism in this world already. Make it shine, make it wow, make it art.": "好工具之所以美，是因为它们是对的。刀刃最完美的弧线，也是最优雅的弧线，所以我们要把那个 TUI 的利落线条打磨到位，把圆角调对，把 CLIs 擦亮。颜色要协调。边距要刚刚好。这个世界上的低饱和粗野主义已经够多了。让它发光，让它惊艳，让它成为艺术。",
  "Excellence is not born out of committee, and Omarchy is not a democracy. It&#39;s a benevolent dictatorship in the grand tradition of Linux, Ruby, and Rails. The dictator&#39;s job is to listen to everyone, but make the call according to their intuition, vision, and experience. Some calls will be wrong, and then they&#39;ll be reverted. Others will be delegated. But the buck will always have a place to stop.": "卓越不是靠委员会开出来的，Omarchy 也不是民主制。它是延续 Linux、Ruby 和 Rails 光荣传统的开明独裁。独裁者的工作是听取所有人的意见，再凭直觉、愿景和经验拍板。有些决定会是错的，错了就回滚。有些会授权出去。但责任永远有地方落脚。",
  "The original hacker cred was all about the code. It didn&#39;t care who you were, what your background was, or even if you were legally old enough to operate a <a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2096542976683970838\">three-node elite BBS out of your bedroom</a>. It just cared about the work, the art, the dare. Omarchy is bringing that ethos back, and dropping the Code-of-Conduct struggle sessions and identity-overload nonsense that has plagued open source for far too long. We&#39;re done with all of it. Just be nice and sincere.": "最初的黑客信誉只关乎代码。不在乎你是谁、什么背景，甚至不在乎你是否到了能合法在自己卧室里运营<a href=\"https://x.com/dhh/status/2096542976683970838\">三节点精英 BBS</a>的年龄。只在乎作品、在乎艺术、在乎胆量。Omarchy 正在把这种精神带回来，抛掉困扰开源太久的 Code-of-Conduct 批斗会和身份过载那套把戏。我们受够了。就好好做人，真诚待人。"
}
